ed volatility of 71% and a beta of 1.40, it amplifies market moves, though its beta has shifted (1y 1.23 vs 5y 1.72), so read it loosely.","About $35.5M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 53% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 97% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $88.18 (margin of safety -2%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 13%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $55.22 to $148 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Technology peers: EV/EBITDA 26.3 vs 16.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 54% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.8% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $132 on average, 46% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 46% clears the cost of capital of 12.3% by 34pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.19).","It runs a 41% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 13.0% of revenue on R&D and 2.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $304.4M.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 7.2, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 4.77).","Working capital ties up about 300 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -3.0% over 3 years, 12.1% over 5 years and 10.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 30%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 11.4% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 21%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (1.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 22, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $2.3M sold).","It returns 4.3% a year to shareholders (4.3% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 1,465 employees, each generates about $573K of revenue, 1.5x the Technology median, and revenue has grown 7.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $73K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.2M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $14K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":73,"head":"Watch: composite 52, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety and the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread); it becomes a buy below $74.95.","pros":["Composite 52, above the 39 line (gates 13/26)","ROIC 46.0% vs WACC 12.3%","FCF margin 12.8%","Revenue grew 12.1%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $304.4M"],"cons":["Trades 2% above fair value of $88.18","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","EV/EBITDA 26.3x vs sector 16.1x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)"],"buy_below":74.95,"vc":{"base":88.18,"base_src":"dcf","bear":55.22,"bull":147.87,"alt_median":56.33,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.5655,"dispersion":0.1294,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","DCF is 57% above the other models' median ($56.33)"]},"med":{"pe":24.3759,"ev_ebitda":16.132,"pfcf":23.2596,"pb":3.2577,"roic":0.075,"gross_margin":0.4677,"fcf_margin":0.1222,"div_yield":0.0137}},"mc_quantiles":[39.